            <ArticleTitle>Common geography as a clue to causation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>117-24</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Certain diseases characteristic of modern civilization have been shown to have a similar worldwide geographical distribution, and in developing countries a similar socio-economic distribution. This suggests that some causative factor may be common to each, and evidence is provided to support the hypothesis that this might be the over-refining of carbohydrate foods.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
